{"task":"T-0596","file":"ci/checks/rights-ui-anti-case.sh","owner":"T-0572","decision":"ADR-T0596-lock-harden.md-§7-eco1-project-root-fix","sanctioned_by":"founder","note":"Fixes ECO-1 (T-0576 test-report finding, notes.ECO-1_foreign_check_bug): PROJECT_ROOT resolved to ${SCRIPT_DIR}/.. = <repo>/ci (one level short of repo root) instead of ${SCRIPT_DIR}/../.. (matching read-pdp-anti-case.sh:26 and anti-case-lock.sh:70) -- the git diff/ls-files pathspec web/src/ therefore resolved against a nonexistent ci/web/src/, the scan was ALWAYS empty, and the gate was structurally always-green regardless of diff content (proved live in T-0576 test-phase: an untracked web/src/ plant with a denylist literal passed exit 0). GROUNDS for founder-class (not auto_additive/FF-FCI13): the fix MUTATES the VALUE of an existing line (PROJECT_ROOT assignment), which fails auto-sanction-additive.sh A-1 (byte-identical line preservation) by construction -- the auto_additive channel is structurally unavailable for a value-fix on an existing line, same governance class as the T-0576 sanction of http-route-auth-coverage.sh FF-0328-3 (also a founder-class modification of an existing predicate, not a pure addition). SCOPE: exactly one line (line 25, the PROJECT_ROOT assignment); FORBIDDEN_LITERALS, scan_diff, self_test, resolve_base_ref untouched. RESTORATION not weakening: the fix takes the gate from \"scan pathspec never resolves, always PASS\" to \"scan resolves against the real repo root, diff-scoped as originally designed (T-0572 spec NF-4)\" -- it STRICTLY INCREASES enforcement; there is no input on which the fixed gate can produce a false-positive relative to the old (structurally-vacuous) behaviour. VERIFIED live (T-0596 BUILD phase, docs/specs/T-0596-lock-harden.spec.md AC-4/AC-5/AC-6): --self-test PASS (synthetic temp-repo fixtures unaffected by the real-PROJECT_ROOT fix); production run on the clean task/T-0596-lock-harden branch PASS exit 0 (diff-scoped semantics correctly does not flag R-4's pre-existing single-quoted web/src/ occurrences, which are not in this branch's diff); a NEW untracked web/src/ plant (e-orlov literal) correctly FAILS exit 1 post-fix, proving the pathspec now resolves to the real tree."}
{"task":"T-0596","file":"ci/checks/anti-case-lock.sh","owner":"T-0576","decision":"ADR-T0596-lock-harden.md-R4-R5-harden","sanctioned_by":"founder","note":"W2/замок-харден follow-up to T-0576 (own file header still reads T-0576, per frozen-checks-immutable.sh ownership-by-header-TID convention -- each task that hardens a file keeps its own sanction entry, same precedent as dual-control-isolation.sh T-0570/T-0573/T-0575 and http-route-auth-coverage.sh T-0575/T-0576). Closes two OPEN, non-blocking findings from the T-0576 review (docs/review/T-0576.review.json R-4 major, R-5 minor): (1) R-4 quote-agnostic harden -- count_literal() matcher widened from double-quote-only to a character class covering double/single/backtick quotes, because web/src/ convention is single quotes and the double-quote-only matcher was blind to 5 real pre-existing code-only occurrences there (role-approver in screen-inbox.jsx:835; approvalRequired x4 in gateway-condition-panel.jsx + screen-dmn-editor.jsx); baseline recounted as FACT by running the new matcher on this branch HEAD (role-approver 2->3, approvalRequired 1->5, aggregate 19->24 -- see ci/checks/data/anti-case-baseline.json). (2) R-5 rc>=2 harden -- count_literal()/read_baseline() outer grep stage no longer blankets rc>=2 (real grep error: missing/unreadable root) under the same || true that legitimately absorbs rc=1 (no-match, the R-1 zero-safety fix); rc>=2 is now FATAL with an explicit message, closing the fail-open risk R-5 flagged. GROUNDS for founder-class (not auto_additive/FF-FCI13): both fixes MUTATE existing lines (the count_literal grep pattern itself, several explanatory comments) rather than purely append new ones -- auto-sanction-additive.sh A-1 (byte-identical line preservation) fails by construction, so the auto_additive channel is structurally unavailable; same governance class as the existing T-0575/T-0576 sanctions on this lineage. SCOPE: header comment block (methodology notes) + count_literal()/read_baseline() bodies + 9 new/expanded --self-test assertions; run_denylist_scan(), LITERALS array, Phase 1/Phase 2 orchestration, and the production-check tail are untouched. VERIFIED live (T-0596 BUILD phase): --self-test 9/9 PASS (5 pre-existing + 2 new quote-agnostic + 2 new rc>=2-fatal assertions); production run on this branch HEAD PASS exit 0 with the recounted baseline; two consecutive production runs byte-identical (idempotency)."}
